  "question": {
    "text": "A big drop is formed by coalescing <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1000</mn></math> small droplets of water. The surface energy will become :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "9s4nP",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn></math> times",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "fkIh9",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> times",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "meSOk",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mi>th</mi></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "XSCyH",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mi>th</mi></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Lets say radius of small droplets is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math> and that of big drop is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>. Total volume of the drops will remains unchanged. Therefore, </p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>r</mi></math></p><p>Now, initial surface energy is, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo> </mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and the final surface energy is, </p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo> </mo><mi>S</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>S</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Clearly, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></math>.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
